WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
Unit 3 is the cadence
and the evidence package.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:05.396
The cadence is design guidance,

3
00:00:05.396 --> 00:00:10.012
from the day-two runbook in Compliance
Automation and Day-2 Operations.

4
00:00:10.012 --> 00:00:12.626
Monthly, a full run, with the results and

5
00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:15.812
the plan of action and
milestones regenerated.

6
00:00:15.812 --> 00:00:19.903
After each remediation wave,
a run of the affected pillar,

7
00:00:19.903 --> 00:00:23.037
so a fix is closed by
evidence, not by a ticket.

8
00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:25.708
Before a tool upgrade reaches production,

9
00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.301
a run of the new version
in the test tenant.

10
00:00:28.301 --> 00:00:30.350
And quarterly, a trend review.

11
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:35.003
Microsoft's operations guidance for
Global Secure Access includes a weekly

12
00:00:35.003 --> 00:00:39.875
scheduled digest; the guide explains two
cautions before adopting it as written.

13
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:43.673
The evidence package for a run
holds the export and its hash,

14
00:00:43.673 --> 00:00:46.385
the normalized results, the dispositions,

15
00:00:46.385 --> 00:00:51.190
the reviews and exceptions with their
hashes, the register, the comparison,

16
00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:55.060
and the chained records with the
S H A two fifty-six sums file.
